We investigate the eigenvalue statistics of the Hermitian block matrix 
\begin{equation*}
H_{N,p}=\begin{pmatrix}
T_p & V_{p,N}^*\\
V_{N,p} & T_N
\end{pmatrix},
\end{equation*}
where $T_p$ and $T_N$ are complex matrices of size $p\times p$ and $N\times N$ with i.i.d. entries, and $V_{p,N}$ is a $p\times N$ matrix with i.i.d. entries. Assuming that the eigenvalue radius ratios are bounded by a constant and that the diagonal matrices $T_p$ and $T_N$ have distinct imaginary parts, we derive the joint statistics of the eigenvalues from the bulk limit of the $O(N)$ sigma-model.

